od/dhcd/s3fs-public/styles/small/public/images/2026-07/NourishMD%20logo2.png.webp?versionId=wKOM2DX6Njzj1Re2bRXgGfhvmBRzkfY4&amp;X-Amz-Content-Sha256=UNSIGNED-PAYLOAD&amp;X-Amz-Security-Token=IQoJb3JpZ2luX2VjEAcaCXVzLWVhc3QtMSJGMEQCIG2Bh/G8ODVYOM8/dL9oVdf9ZEUOxeTcPDVRBWFEhc73AiB5JOnyIVseRoK3KyUEebsj3EGZctLWUbMDIVjBZxCo0CrDBQjQ//////////8BEAAaDDcxNjA2NzY2Nzk0MiIMDfQYStBy2fHgmYtQKpcFj%2BTSx6P5O8HjHnKvWdj2NC7PRIY14%2BJlWbWxrcQS3DfIDnSEiffoAYlVIE0zuTQVnDQf4XKWZJOM6p5c8A370pwgffNpOrMx7N1jOMCtH2V4Xmh8S0S309EC74tZCYf81UjgcXTFIv2XFVa%2B4Ol5j2f%2BU9Gij36LZcKfrihRmafELwd%2B7%2BVQ0kpGyOrq1aTYN4OagSQmrKKSfLYX4nIIMyWBstVoeta30fKJK0SelBI7u4%2BzGO1%2BuL48g%2BuEHNMeWOVuKfw5RxE8XjhmcjQKPxHfrQetccflBV3AUUx0IHbqvJ5KbR/DwjinQrO3kZDuZZcLogcB2EQwy6ihoP6V2M7MWh90dcUFkgBrg0j3UbNb6hXWVDU9mQKxnlDKV8imOLbk4dszpn%2BZjEu4xPdw9BteL7YZFhRIMrAoyN05fOtf1PgUxZjtYkA9z97qPsXKUtx3GRfm89xApNt0F35Gzvjqptf0jUzXD0Ud370fbdknx7XVVnlOJcS9IT1uqsbvcYSWn47MimAdEkK1LAJNThl6pYq5ROyvSfrk302LhomFmSsW3WNjW3mriRmXXBLVYqQTjIQRWVIkMrCzvcKiDCg%2BAszhApMAxJcsy9QCaVWvc7ZizxcLtS8udDmpFqYJHC1kiudfUykks3KPnNHolDO7vcIPc2zivJmKZmWo%2BIz%2Bf0rHNxkwD/kPEzYjJboPRnYhrzUa6g8%2BMvPs4VjNuAtTMBqIGWR/5ViWp6NRfTt%2Boc9jex9sSNDwsXF7%2BGINUS2cAIVFiyndbLqodEAVBnes4CMknnPONvHZViKZtilZVIgFAclqKoE7p0ENGWojrmbhlY2EHaNRw3ElO5jeNp9%2BNFIKfYnLrw5YyQjcm%2BrRCLfXPpOfMIvVw9YGOrIBCBzzs5YUHrdABRWZwv9lwncfXRczF2XVoXc3OGFIw/UMLPbbKLMZ3LKt/3SBDS7hY%2Br6s5JjTOElAtOMRBZT9eLHhpYGaRumozdq3oLDgql3SEyqLjPfZuZRTmT48fWLRyveRxpoDSf5e81o6Uoz1u6lsKnPRGFm9mXS0rMLYHNwuD9ZLxn6khAC3cmaAZdXmQebM/fE/Ce/haU20m3jutlFVDnrcRYM%2B3QJGlFj7BWH1Q%3D%3D&amp;X-Amz-Algorithm=AWS4-HMAC-SHA256&amp;X-Amz-Credential=ASIA2NOHVP7TDQ5BOYWE/20261015/us-east-1/s3/aws4_request&amp;X-Amz-Date=20261015T152232Z&amp;X-Amz-SignedHeaders=host&amp;X-Amz-Expires=600&amp;X-Amz-Signature=54936fbb3d4b59ab102b41c199e43ad2c2be9dde5c9ca6bb232b96013e5d5124&amp;itok=IEpoG46F\" width=\"175\"/>\n<figcaption></figcaption>\n</figure>\n<p> </p><p>The Nouri​shMD Grant Program is a targeted investment designed to expand access to healthy and fresh foods in Maryland communities experiencing food insecurity by providing direct grants to eligible retailers. </p><h2 dir=\"ltr\">Available funding</h2><ul><li dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Grant size:</strong> $25,000 – $150,000</li><li dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Total funding available:</strong> Up to $3.67 million ($2 million in state funds and $1.67 million in federal <a class=\"maryland-link\" href=\"https://health.maryland.gov/pophealth/Pages/Rural-Health-Transformation-Program.aspx\">Rural Health Transformation Program funds​</a>)</li></ul><h2 dir=\"ltr\">Eligible applicants</h2><p dir=\"ltr\">For-profit or nonprofit food retailers that:</p><ul><li dir=\"ltr\">Serve a community with a <a class=\"maryland-link\" href=\"https://compass.maryland.gov/\">Maryland Community Compass (MCC)​</a> Fresh Food Gap Score of 65% or higher<ul><li dir=\"ltr\"><a class=\"maryland-link\" href=\"https://youtu.be/KU7Y6tmh1LY\">Watch: How to Find Your Community's Fresh Food Gap Score​</a></li></ul></li><li dir=\"ltr\">Operate at least 5 days per week, year round (farmer'​s markets/on-farm markets exempt from 5-day requirement and must operate 10 months out of the year)</li><li dir=\"ltr\">Currently or plan to offer fresh, frozen, or minimally processed healthy foods</li><li dir=\"ltr\">Dedicate at least 20% of inventory or food-sales space to healthy food items</li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\">Please refer to the <a class=\"maryland-link\" data-entity-substitution=\"canonical\" data-entity-type=\"media\" data-entity-uuid=\"ae412535-6706-43d6-8f76-860d9f8e1e68\" href=\"/media/4422\" title=\"RFA NourishMD Round 2\">Request for Applications (RFA) - PDF - 172.79 KB</a> for a complete list of eligibility requirements.</p><p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Tip:</strong> Visit the <a class=\"maryland-link\" href=\"https://compass.maryland.gov/\">Maryland Community Compass (MCC)​</a> to learn more, use data insights to identify new opportunities, and connect with expert resources to help your business thrive.</p><h3>Eligible retailers</h3><p dir=\"ltr\">Eligible retailers include:</p><ul><li dir=\"ltr\">Grocery stores</li><li dir=\"ltr\">Corner stores</li><li dir=\"ltr\">Farm stands and other on-farm markets</li><li dir=\"ltr\">Farmers' markets</li><li dir=\"ltr\">Community Supported Agriculture (CSA, using an average FFGS for delivery area)</li><li dir=\"ltr\">Food co-ops</li><li dir=\"ltr\">Delivery retailers serving a population with low fresh food access</li><li dir=\"ltr\">Small retail stores where the majority of inventory or sales are food-related (provided no more than 25% of gross sales are derived from alcohol/tobacco products)</li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\">To qualify for Rural Health Transformation Program funds, the retailer must be located in a <a class=\"maryland-link\" href=\"https://health.maryland.gov/pophealth/Documents/Rural%20Health/RHTP/Rural%20Maryland%20State%20Designated%20Counties.pdf\">designated rural county - PDF</a></p><h2>Eligible use of funds</h2><p dir=\"ltr\">Use of funds depends on the source of funding, though dually-sourced awards are available.</p><h3>State funds</h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>$2 million</strong> in State funds may be used to directly support improved healthy food access, including:</p><ul><li dir=\"ltr\">Purchase of furniture, fixtures, and/or equipment (e.g., Energy Star-rated refrigeration, shelving, etc.)</li><li dir=\"ltr\">Renovation, build-out, and facility upgrades</li><li dir=\"ltr\">Capital needs related to inventory expansion (non-prepared foods)</li><li dir=\"ltr\">Working capital involved with expansion or renovations/construction</li><li dir=\"ltr\">Infrastructure and technology for SNAP/EBT setup</li><li dir=\"ltr\">Purchase of a vehicle for fresh food delivery</li><li dir=\"ltr\">Commercial solar installations or heat pumps to reduce operating costs</li></ul><h3>Rural Health Transformation Program (RHTP) funds</h3><p><strong>$1.67 million</strong> in RHTP funds can be used to directly support improved healthy food access, including:</p><ul><li dir=\"ltr\">Purchase of furniture, fixtures, and/or equipment (e.g., Energy Star-rated refrigeration, shelving, etc.)</li><li dir=\"ltr\">Facility upgrades to support cold storage or point of sale expansion ONLY (ie. electrical upgrade for a new walk-in, grant year WIFI costs for POS terminal usage, cement slab for new walk-in)</li><li dir=\"ltr\">Infrastructure and technology for SNAP/EBT setup</li><li dir=\"ltr\">Marketing costs to promote the RHTP funded efforts only (Please note, pre-approval for these expenses is required)</li><li dir=\"ltr\">Purchase of a vehicle for fresh food delivery</li><li dir=\"ltr\">Electrical installations or heat pumps to reduce operating costs</li><li dir=\"ltr\">Expenses related to pre-harvest infrastructure are not eligible for any grant funding under this grant program </li></ul><h2 dir=\"ltr\">Program timeline</h2><ul><li dir=\"ltr\"><p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>September 10, 2026</strong>: Soft launch and virtual information sessions, see below for registration links.</p></li><li dir=\"ltr\"><p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>September 22, 2026</strong>: Official launch; Tier 1 Application Portal opens (12:00 p.m. EST).</p></li><li dir=\"ltr\"><p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>November 2, 2026</strong>: Tier 1 Application Portal closes (5:00 p.m. EST).</p></li><li dir=\"ltr\"><p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>February 4, 2027</strong>: Tier 2 Application Portal closes (5:00 p.m. EST).</p></li><li dir=\"ltr\"><p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>February – March 2027</strong>: Tier 2 Review &amp; Funding Recommendations finalized.</p></li><li dir=\"ltr\"><p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>April 2027</strong>: Award Notifications and funding approvals.</p></li><li dir=\"ltr\"><p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>May 2027</strong>: Execution of grant agreements and fund disbursement.</p></li><li dir=\"ltr\"><p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>May 2028</strong>: End of grant period and final deliverable deadline. </p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\">All interested applicants must submit an application by November 2, 2026. Only applicants that meet the baseline requirements in Tier 1 will advance to the Tier 2 application.</p><h2 dir=\"ltr\">Two-tiered application process</h2><p>The Round 2 grant cycle features a new, two-step application process to make things simpler and faster for everyone.</p><h3 dir=\"ltr\">Tier 1: Eligibility and triage</h3><p dir=\"ltr\">The objective of the Tier 1 application is to verify baseline eligibility and measure community need before applicants invest significant resources required for a full grant proposal.</p><ul><li dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Eligibility floor:</strong> All projects must meet an absolute Fresh Food Gap Score (FFGS) floor of 65. Applications with a score below 65 will be removed through an automated binary check during submission. <a class=\"maryland-link\" href=\"https://compass.maryland.gov/methodology/\">View Fresh Food Gap Score Methodology</a> for more information.</li><li dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Use of grant funds: </strong>This section will include a business overview, and an overview/needs statement for the use of grant funds. Detailed breakout of RHTP/GO Bond fund requests will be completed by the applicant in Tier 2, with assistance provided as needed.</li></ul><h3 dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Tier 2: Comprehensive project evaluation</strong></h3><p dir=\"ltr\">Applicants who successfully pass the Tier 1 triage and receive leadership approval will be invited to submit a full Tier 2 application. This phase requires detailed documentation to ensure project viability and administrative compliance.</p><p><strong>Submission requirements:</strong></p><ul><li dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Project narratives:</strong> Comprehensive descriptions of the project, including its impact on fresh food access and a breakout of RHTP and GO Bond funded expenses.</li><li dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Line-item budgets:</strong> Detailed expense budgets including vendor quotes and unverified cost assumptions.</li><li dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Governance &amp; Compliance Documents:</strong><ul><li dir=\"ltr\">Articles of Incorporation and Organization By-Laws.</li><li dir=\"ltr\">SDAT proof of good standing, State tax registration documentation, IRS W-9 Form (name must match exactly).</li><li dir=\"ltr\">Mandatory disclosure for active bankruptcy or litigation.</li><li dir=\"ltr\">Any additional documentation that may be required by DHCD.</li><li dir=\"ltr\">RHTP Applicants Only: Attestation regarding duplication and supplantation.</li></ul></li></ul><h2 dir=\"ltr\">How to apply</h2><p>Submit the online application before November 2, 2026. Please review the <a class=\"maryland-link\" data-entity-substitution=\"canonical\" data-entity-type=\"media\" data-entity-uuid=\"5352ea27-9483-46fc-87c0-f39b062c5c76\" href=\"/media/4512\" title=\"NourishMD Grant Application User Guide\">Tier 1 Application User Guide - PDF - 73.51 KB</a> before completing the online application.</p>\n<div class=\"maryland-button-group grid-container\">\n<h2 class=\"maryland-button-group__title usa-sr-only\" id=\"button-group\"><span>NourishMD How to apply</span>\n</h2>\n<ul aria-labelledby=\"button-group\" class=\"usa-button-group maryland-button-group__list\">\n<li class=\"usa-button-group__item maryland-button-group__item\">\n<a class=\"usa-button maryland-button-group__button\" href=\"https://app.letspresta.com/signup/39/117\">\n            Complete the online application form\n          </a>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h2 dir=\"ltr\">Engagement strategy</h2><ul><li><a class=\"maryland-link\" href=\"https://youtu.be/mfM7q5CpKpU?si=CbGRz6Wqzx-EhhJK\">September 18, 2026 NourishMD Round 2 Informational Webinar recording</a></li><li><a class=\"maryland-link\" href=\"https://youtu.be/msGxe0av9dA?si=1SLFtOKAtwdE20QD\">September 21, 2026 NourishMD Round 2 Informational Webinar recording</a></li><li><a class=\"maryland-link\" href=\"https://youtu.be/mT5x6y1vZ5E?si=E7yPWAtAVNAPqwxv\">Southern Maryland NourishMD Round 2 Informational Webinar recording</a></li><li><a class=\"maryland-link\" href=\"https://youtu.be/2aingw4Iejw?si=osaBIeRJI_akKGK0\">Central Maryland NourishMD Round 2 Informational Webinar recording</a></li></ul><h2>Other funding sources</h2><p dir=\"ltr\">Applicants that are jointly eligible for both programs and apply to both will receive priority consideration for awards from each program, subject to available funding and program eligibility requirements.</p><h3 dir=\"ltr\">Beyond Direct Grants: DHCD Business Lending Options</h3><p dir=\"ltr\">NourishMD serves as a vetting engine for broader state of Maryland business development initiatives. Applicants may also be evaluated for direct loan products and companion lending through the <strong>Business Lending</strong> program. A checkbox is provided in the application for those interested in exploring these flexible lending options. Note: Indicating an interest in your application for these programs does not guarantee acceptance or an award of funding from DHCD.</p><h3 dir=\"ltr\">Maryland Market Money (MMM) partnership</h3><p dir=\"ltr\">In partnership with the Maryland Department of Agriculture, NourishMD applicants will be considered for coordinated funding opportunities through both programs. MMM provides a dollar-for-dollar match for purchases made using federal nutrition benefits at participating Maryland farmers markets, farm stands, and other on-farm retailers, while also providing technical assistance, training, marketing, and other support to participating businesses.</p><p dir=\"ltr\">Currently participating MMM Access Points are encouraged to apply for NourishMD funding. New NourishMD applicants seeking to become MMM participants will be prioritized for MMM participation as funding becomes available. Farmers markets and on-farm retailers seeking technical assistance to accept SNAP/EBT may indicate this in their NourishMD application and will be connected with MDA for assistance with the process.</p><p dir=\"ltr\"><a class=\"maryland-link\" href=\"https://www.marylandmarketmoney.org/\">Visit Maryland Market Money (MMM)</a></p><h3>Maryland Department of Health's Healthy Corner Store Program </h3><p dir=\"ltr\">This program provides grants to establish relationships between local health departments and small scale retail stores in Maryland recognized rural districts, recognize those establishments that are stocking healthy products, and recommend areas for improvement for retailers to meet the criteria of a Healthy Maryland Corner Store. For more information.</p><h2 dir=\"ltr\">For more information</h2><ul><li dir=\"ltr\"><a class=\"maryland-link\" href=\"https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScwmB55D1ABdZ_4d7Vb7lkXlK8QnKk6cjNYuPJU84ErtMfeIQ/viewform\">Schedule a NourishMD consultation</a>: The NourishMD team is available for one on one consultations until 5pm on Tuesday, February 2nd.</li><li>Email us at <a class=\"maryland-link\" href=\"​dhcd.businesslending@maryland.gov​​\">​<span class=\"__cf_email__\" data-cfemail=\"44202c27206a2631372d2a21373728212a202d2a23042925363d28252a206a232b32\">[email protected]</span>​​</a></li></ul>\n<section aria-labelledby=\"automatic-list-1002\" class=\"maryland-automatic-list\">\n<div class=\"maryland-card-group__header\">\n<div class=\"maryland-card-group__header-content\">\n<h2 class=\"maryland-card-group__title\" id=\"automatic-list-1002\"><span>Business Development news</span>\n</h2>\n</div>\n<div class=\"maryland-card-group__more-link\">\n<a class=\"maryland-link\" href=\"/news-stories\">\n          See all news\n        </a>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div><div class=\"views-element-container\" id=\"block-views-block-automatic-list-blocks-content-block-automatic-list-news\">\n<div><div class=\"js-view-dom-id-cb3e5e44815b58218895503a582d3bfc3679cc81654dae478c8a63da2b92d234\">\n<ul class=\"maryland-card-group\">\n<li class=\"maryland-card maryland-card--linked\" id=\"auto-list-item\">\n<a aria-label=\"&lt;span&gt;Governor Moore Announces Fiscal Year 2027 Application 